<h1>select k<sup>th</sup> element</h1>
<p>
(classic problem)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
Find the k<sup>th</sup> smallest element of a set.  Two approaches are a modified <a href="distributionSort.html"><em>distribution sort</em></a> or  <a href="selectAndPartition.html"><em>select and partition</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Also known as</strong> selection problem, find k<sup>th</sup> least element, k<sup>th</sup> smallest element.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="select.html"><em>Select</em></a>, <a href="modifind.html"><em>MODIFIND</em></a>, <a href="find.html"><em>Find</em></a>, <a href="reservoirSampling.html"><em>reservoir sampling</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
The select-and-partition approximately divides in half the number of elements that must be considered at each step.  The modified distribution sort divides by m the number of elements at each step.  The latter is faster, but the former is more generally applicable.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

